diagnosis_text:
Thorough end-to-end investigation found no fault anywhere in the Kath2 topology. Every office-LAN host (office_pc 192.168.3.2, exam_cell 192.168.3.3, enquiry 192.168.3.4, tpo 192.168.3.5) can successfully reach the Server Room (pc1 at 1.0.0.5) and every tested Internet Lab host (pc2 at 128.168.0.2) with full packet delivery and TTL-consistent hop counts of 62, exactly as expected through router1→router2. The RIP routing plane is fully healthy: router1 holds learned routes to 1.0.0.0/8 and 128.168.0.0/16 via 20.20.0.2 (eth3), router2 holds the return route to 192.168.3.0/24 via 20.20.0.1 (eth2), and all routes are stable (5+ minutes old, not flapping). The ripd, zebra, and watchfrr daemons on all three routers started at 04:09 and have been running continuously without restarts. Router1's forwarding plane is clean: iptables FORWARD chain is empty (policy ACCEPT) and ip_forward is enabled. All interface IPs match the expected addressing scheme and all links show UP/LOWER_UP. The WAN link wan_r1_r2 between router1 and router2 is reachable with sub-millisecond RTT. The reported symptom — Office PCs unable to reach the Server Room and Internet Lab — does not exist in the live lab. The ticket describes a non-existent outage; no corrective action is required.
=== END ===